{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And a woman to her sister you shall not take.</b> As if it said 'you shall not lie with,' for Scripture sometimes designates relations by the term שכיבה (lying), sometimes by the term קיחה (taking), and sometimes by the term ידיעה (knowing) — for one cannot say that this 'taking' means betrothal by money but that without money for betrothal it is permitted, since it is in fact forbidden to lie with a woman and her sister in any manner. And likewise in the section of the consecrated (Leviticus 20:14) it is written: ״ואיש אשר יקח את אשה ואת אמה זמה היא״ — 'And a man who takes a woman and her mother, it is depravity'; and ״איש אשר יקח את אחותו״ — 'a man who takes his sister'; and ״איש אשר יקח את אשת אחיו״ — 'a man who takes his brother's wife' — the sense of all of them being 'who lies with.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:30.507379460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}